{
 "esm": "1.1.0",
 "metadata": {
  "name": "NoahPotentialEvaporation",
  "description": "Linearised Penman potential evaporation of WRF's unified Noah land-surface model, SUBROUTINE PENMAN of phys/module_sf_noahlsm.F (WRF 4.8, sf_surface_physics = 2), together with the partial sums rch, rr, t24 and epsca that PENMAN passes back for the rest of SFLX to reuse. Penman (1948) combination form, linearised about the air temperature: epsca = (a rr + rad delta)/(delta + rr), where a = elcp1 (q2sat - q2) is the vapour-pressure deficit expressed as a temperature, rad = fnet/rch + th2 - sfctmp the available-energy term likewise, delta = elcp1 dqsdt2 the saturation slope and rr the radiative-plus-aerodynamic resistance ratio; etp = epsca rch / lvs. Snow blends two latent heats through the snow-cover fraction sncovr: elcp1 and lvs both interpolate between the liquid (lsubc) and the ice (lsubs) value, so that over full snow cover the potential flux is a sublimation. Falling precipitation adds its own sensible-heat capacity to rr -- cph2o for rain, cpice for snow -- and freezing rain adds the latent heat of fusion released on impact as flx2 = -lsubf prcp, which is subtracted from the net radiation. THREE things a consumer must know. (1) The `ssoil` this routine subtracts from the net radiation is NOT the ground heat flux SHFLX returns at the end of the step; it is the flux diagnosed from the INCOMING skin temperature, ssoil = df1 (t1 - stc[1])/(0.5 |zsoil[1]|), which SFLX computes just before the call. (2) PENMAN declares its OWN cp = 1004.6, which disagrees with the cp = 1004.5 that module_model_constants supplies to every other routine in the same module (FORTRAN_BUGS N88); it enters only through rho -> rch. (3) The radiative term of rr is the hard-coded literal 6.48e-8 standing for 4 sigma rd / cp, whose exact value with Noah's own sigma and rd is 6.48048e-8 -- a 7.4e-5 relative difference that this component reproduces by keeping the literal, because the object here is WRF's answer and not the exact one (FORTRAN_BUGS N89). The UA_PHYS canopy-shading branch (flx4, etpn) is not transcribed: it is off in both reference runs and is a separate parameterization. The component is algebraic in the consumer's state and owns nothing.",
  "license": "MIT",
  "tags": ["wrf", "land-surface", "noah", "penman", "potential-evaporation", "surface-energy-balance"],
  "references": [
   {"citation": "Penman, H. L. (1948). Natural evaporation from open water, bare soil and grass. Proc. R. Soc. Lond. A, 193, 120-145."},
   {"citation": "Mahrt, F., and M. Ek (1984). The influence of atmospheric stability on potential evaporation. J. Climate Appl. Meteor., 23, 222-234."},
   {"citation": "Chen, F., and J. Dudhia (2001). Coupling an advanced land surface-hydrology model with the Penn State-NCAR MM5 modeling system. Part I. Mon. Wea. Rev., 129, 569-585."},
   {"citation": "wrf-model/WRF v4.8.0 phys/module_sf_noahlsm.F SUBROUTINE PENMAN lines 2195-2312, called from SFLX line 735 (instrumented in ctessum-claude/WRF branch earthsciml-instrumented-chem170, commit ac6d4cc)."}
  ]
 },
 "models": {
  "NoahPotentialEvaporation": {
   "subsystems": {
    "par": {"ref": "./noah_parameters.esm"}
   },
   "variables": {
    "sfctmp": {"type": "parameter", "units": "K", "default": 300.0,
     "description": "Air temperature at the lowest model level, WRF's SFCTMP."},
    "sfcprs": {"type": "parameter", "units": "Pa", "default": 100000.0,
     "description": "Air pressure at the lowest model level, WRF's SFCPRS."},
    "th2": {"type": "parameter", "units": "K", "default": 300.0,
     "description": "Potential temperature at the lowest model level referenced to the surface pressure, WRF's TH2, supplied by the driver."},
    "q2": {"type": "parameter", "units": "kg/kg", "default": 0.01,
     "description": "Specific humidity at the lowest model level, WRF's Q2."},
    "q2sat": {"type": "parameter", "units": "kg/kg", "default": 0.02,
     "description": "Saturation specific humidity at the lowest model level, WRF's Q2SAT."},
    "dqsdt2": {"type": "parameter", "units": "kg/(kg*K)", "default": 0.001,
     "description": "Slope of the saturation specific humidity with temperature at the lowest model level, WRF's DQSDT2."},
    "ch": {"type": "parameter", "units": "m/s", "default": 0.01,
     "description": "Surface exchange coefficient for heat and moisture from the surface-layer scheme, WRF's CH."},
    "prcp": {"type": "parameter", "units": "kg/(m^2*s)", "default": 0.0,
     "description": "Precipitation rate reaching the surface, WRF's PRCP. Enters only through the sensible-heat capacity of the falling hydrometeors."},
    "fdown": {"type": "parameter", "units": "W/m^2", "default": 600.0,
     "description": "Total absorbed downward radiation at the surface, WRF's FDOWN = solnet + lwdn (net shortwave plus DOWNWARD longwave; the upward longwave is the emissi sigma t24 term subtracted below)."},
    "ssoil": {"type": "parameter", "units": "W/m^2", "default": 0.0,
     "description": "Ground heat flux diagnosed from the INCOMING skin temperature, df1 (t1 - stc[1])/(0.5 |zsoil[1]|), positive downward into the soil. SFLX computes this immediately before calling PENMAN; it is NOT the ssoil that SHFLX returns after the step."},
    "emissi": {"type": "parameter", "units": "1", "default": 0.985,
     "description": "Surface emissivity, WRF's EMISSI."},
    "sncovr": {"type": "parameter", "units": "1", "default": 0.0,
     "description": "Fraction of the grid cell covered by snow, WRF's SNCOVR. Blends the liquid and ice latent heats in elcp1 and lvs."},
    "aoasis": {"type": "parameter", "units": "1", "default": 1.0,
     "description": "Oasis-effect multiplier on a POSITIVE epsca, WRF's AOASIS (1 = off, the default and the value in both reference runs)."},
    "snowing": {"type": "parameter", "units": "1", "default": 0.0,
     "description": "Indicator (1/0) for WRF's SNOWNG, set by the driver when the precipitation reaching the ground is frozen. Selects cpice rather than cph2o for the hydrometeor heat capacity, and removes the prcp > 0 guard that the rain branch carries."},
    "freezing_rain": {"type": "parameter", "units": "1", "default": 0.0,
     "description": "Indicator (1/0) for WRF's FRZGRA, set by the driver when liquid precipitation falls onto a below-freezing surface. Activates flx2."},
    "t2v": {"type": "unknown", "units": "K",
     "description": "Virtual temperature at the lowest model level, sfctmp (1 + 0.61 q2), used for the air density."},
    "rho": {"type": "unknown", "units": "kg/m^3",
     "description": "Air density at the lowest model level, sfcprs/(rd t2v), with Noah's rd = 287.04."},
    "rch": {"type": "unknown", "units": "W/(m^2*K)",
     "description": "Bulk heat-transfer coefficient in energy units, rho cp ch. PENMAN's own cp = 1004.6 enters here and nowhere else (FORTRAN_BUGS N88)."},
    "elcp1": {"type": "unknown", "units": "J/kg",
     "description": "Snow-weighted (L/cp) group, (1 - sncovr) elcp + sncovr elcp lsubs/lvh2o; equals elcp over snow-free ground."},
    "lvs": {"type": "unknown", "units": "J/kg",
     "description": "Snow-weighted latent heat, (1 - sncovr) lvh2o + sncovr lsubs; equals lvh2o over snow-free ground."},
    "t24": {"type": "unknown", "units": "K^4",
     "description": "Fourth power of the air temperature, sfctmp^4, the linearisation point of the surface longwave emission."},
    "delta": {"type": "unknown", "units": "1",
     "description": "Saturation-humidity slope in the Penman combination, elcp1 dqsdt2."},
    "rr_rad": {"type": "unknown", "units": "1",
     "description": "Radiative part of the resistance ratio, emissi t24 6.48e-8/(sfcprs ch) + 1. The literal 6.48e-8 stands for 4 sigma rd/cp and is kept as WRF writes it (FORTRAN_BUGS N89)."},
    "rr": {"type": "unknown", "units": "1",
     "description": "Resistance ratio including the sensible-heat capacity of falling precipitation: rr_rad + cph2o prcp/rch for rain, + cpice prcp/rch for snow."},
    "flx2": {"type": "unknown", "units": "W/m^2",
     "description": "Latent heat released by freezing rain on impact, -lsubf prcp when freezing_rain is set and zero otherwise. Subtracted from fnet."},
    "fnet": {"type": "unknown", "units": "W/m^2",
     "description": "Net energy available at the surface for the potential-evaporation estimate, fdown - emissi sigma t24 - ssoil - flx2."},
    "rad": {"type": "unknown", "units": "K",
     "description": "Available energy expressed as a temperature, fnet/rch + th2 - sfctmp."},
    "a": {"type": "unknown", "units": "K",
     "description": "Vapour-pressure deficit expressed as a temperature, elcp1 (q2sat - q2)."},
    "epsca_raw": {"type": "unknown", "units": "K",
     "description": "Penman combination before the oasis multiplier, (a rr + rad delta)/(delta + rr)."},
    "epsca": {"type": "unknown", "units": "K",
     "description": "Penman potential evaporation expressed as a temperature difference, epsca_raw scaled by aoasis where it is positive. Negative epsca means dew."},
    "etp": {"type": "unknown", "units": "kg/(m^2*s)",
     "description": "Potential evaporation as a kinematic (mass) flux, epsca rch / lvs. This is the ETP that NOPAC/SNOPAC divide among the evaporation components."},
    "etp_energy": {"type": "unknown", "units": "W/m^2",
     "description": "The same potential evaporation in energy units, etp ((1 - sncovr) lvh2o + sncovr lsubs), which is the conversion SFLX applies before returning ETP and therefore the quantity WRF reports. Because that factor is exactly lvs, it reduces to epsca rch."}
   },
   "equations": [
    {"lhs": "t2v", "rhs": {"op": "*", "args": ["sfctmp", {"op": "+", "args": [1.0, {"op": "*", "args": [0.61, "q2"]}]}]}},
    {"lhs": "rho", "rhs": {"op": "/", "args": ["sfcprs", {"op": "*", "args": ["par.rd", "t2v"]}]}},
    {"lhs": "rch", "rhs": {"op": "*", "args": [{"op": "*", "args": ["rho", "par.cp_penman"]}, "ch"]}},
    {"lhs": "elcp1", "rhs": {"op": "+", "args": [
      {"op": "*", "args": [{"op": "-", "args": [1.0, "sncovr"]}, "par.elcp"]},
      {"op": "*", "args": [{"op": "*", "args": ["sncovr", "par.elcp"]},
                           {"op": "/", "args": ["par.lsubs", "par.lvh2o"]}]}]}},
    {"lhs": "lvs", "rhs": {"op": "+", "args": [
      {"op": "*", "args": [{"op": "-", "args": [1.0, "sncovr"]}, "par.lvh2o"]},
      {"op": "*", "args": ["sncovr", "par.lsubs"]}]}},
    {"lhs": "t24", "rhs": {"op": "^", "args": ["sfctmp", 4.0]}},
    {"lhs": "delta", "rhs": {"op": "*", "args": ["elcp1", "dqsdt2"]}},
    {"lhs": "rr_rad", "rhs": {"op": "+", "args": [
      {"op": "/", "args": [
        {"op": "*", "args": [{"op": "*", "args": ["emissi", "t24"]}, 6.48e-8]},
        {"op": "*", "args": ["sfcprs", "ch"]}]},
      1.0]}},
    {"lhs": "rr", "rhs": {"op": "ifelse", "args": [
      {"op": "==", "args": ["snowing", 1.0]},
      {"op": "+", "args": ["rr_rad", {"op": "/", "args": [{"op": "*", "args": ["par.cpice", "prcp"]}, "rch"]}]},
      {"op": "ifelse", "args": [
        {"op": ">", "args": ["prcp", 0.0]},
        {"op": "+", "args": ["rr_rad", {"op": "/", "args": [{"op": "*", "args": ["par.cph2o", "prcp"]}, "rch"]}]},
        "rr_rad"]}]}},
    {"lhs": "flx2", "rhs": {"op": "ifelse", "args": [
      {"op": "==", "args": ["freezing_rain", 1.0]},
      {"op": "*", "args": [{"op": "-", "args": [0.0, "par.lsubf"]}, "prcp"]},
      0.0]}},
    {"lhs": "fnet", "rhs": {"op": "-", "args": [
      {"op": "-", "args": [
        {"op": "-", "args": ["fdown", {"op": "*", "args": [{"op": "*", "args": ["emissi", "par.sigma"]}, "t24"]}]},
        "ssoil"]},
      "flx2"]}},
    {"lhs": "rad", "rhs": {"op": "-", "args": [
      {"op": "+", "args": [{"op": "/", "args": ["fnet", "rch"]}, "th2"]}, "sfctmp"]}},
    {"lhs": "a", "rhs": {"op": "*", "args": ["elcp1", {"op": "-", "args": ["q2sat", "q2"]}]}},
    {"lhs": "epsca_raw", "rhs": {"op": "/", "args": [
      {"op": "+", "args": [{"op": "*", "args": ["a", "rr"]}, {"op": "*", "args": ["rad", "delta"]}]},
      {"op": "+", "args": ["delta", "rr"]}]}},
    {"lhs": "epsca", "rhs": {"op": "ifelse", "args": [
      {"op": ">", "args": ["epsca_raw", 0.0]},
      {"op": "*", "args": ["epsca_raw", "aoasis"]},
      "epsca_raw"]}},
    {"lhs": "etp", "rhs": {"op": "/", "args": [{"op": "*", "args": ["epsca", "rch"]}, "lvs"]}},
    {"lhs": "etp_energy", "rhs": {"op": "*", "args": ["etp",
      {"op": "+", "args": [
        {"op": "*", "args": [{"op": "-", "args": [1.0, "sncovr"]}, "par.lvh2o"]},
        {"op": "*", "args": ["sncovr", "par.lsubs"]}]}]}}
   ],
   "tests": [
     {
       "id": "chem170_scm_step1",
       "description": "Reference: WRF 4.8 em_scm_xy single-column run at chem_opt = 170 with Noah (sf_surface_physics = 2), data/eqwefic/chem170_scm, dumped by ctessum-claude/WRF branch earthsciml-instrumented-chem170 and replayed through the real64 (-fdefault-real-8) kernels/noah_driver at ESM_DT = 0.01 s. Inputs are the dumped SFLX arguments (real32 values widened); expected values are the real64 replay. PENMAN runs on the INPUT state, before NOPAC advances anything, so none of these outputs depends on dt. rch, rr, t24, epsca and the ssoil PENMAN is called with are not Registry variables and are published by the kernels/noah_esm_*.inc splices into a build-time copy of module_sf_noahlsm.F (the WRF source is untouched). Snow-free (sncovr = 0), liquid precipitation (snowng = frzgra = .false.), aoasis = 1, ua_phys = .false.: pre-dawn, etp near zero.",
